From 96c3f7fdab4dd06c410b6f933a99053f1d2ffd1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/40] drm/msm/a8xx: use the A8xx GMU keep-alive register in
 the hang IRQ

a8xx_fault_detect_irq() votes for GMU keep-alive so that the GPU stays
powered while the hang state is read and dumped. It writes
REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU_PWR_COL_KEEPALIVE, which is the A6xx/A7xx offset
(0x1f8c3). The A8xx GMU moved the register to 0x1f7e4, which is
REG_A8XX_GMU_GMU_PWR_COL_KEEPALIVE in a6xx_gmu.xml. So on A8xx the vote
never reaches the GMU and a different GMU register is written instead.
With IFPC on A840 the GX can then power collapse while the fault
handler is still reading it.

a6xx_gmu_force_off() already clears the A8xx register when recovery
turns the GMU off, and a8xx_preempt.c uses the A8xx variant of the
preemption keep-alive. Use the A8xx register here as well.

Fixes: 288a93200892 ("drm/msm/adreno: Introduce A8x GPU Support")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
index f892731cd..2bc334644 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
@@ -1149,7 +1149,7 @@ static void a8xx_fault_detect_irq(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	 * collecting information
 	 */
 	if (!adreno_has_gmu_wrapper(adreno_gpu))
-		gmu_write(&a6xx_gpu->gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU_PWR_COL_KEEPALIVE, 1);
+		gmu_write(&a6xx_gpu->gmu, REG_A8XX_GMU_GMU_PWR_COL_KEEPALIVE, 1);
 
 	DRM_DEV_ERROR(&gpu->pdev->dev,
 		"gpu fault ring %d fence %x status %8.8X gfx_status %8.8X\n",
-- 
2.56.0

